<ServiceLayout title="AI Visibility & AEO for Chiropractors | ChiroCandy" description={description} slug="ai-visibility" heroTitle="AI visibility for chiropractic practices" heroAnswer="ChiroCandy is rolling out chiropractic AI visibility and answer engine optimization (AEO) through the GetPatients.com AI visibility package. GetPatients.com is a ChiroCandy company. Talk with our team about the rollout and how the proposed work fits your existing SEO plan." serviceName="Chiropractic AI Visibility and Answer Engine Optimization" dateModified="2026-10-09" faqs={faqs} relatedServices={[{href:'/services/search-engine-optimization/',label:'Chiropractic SEO'},{href:'/services/web-design/',label:'Website design'},{href:'/services/ai-patient-coordinator/',label:'AI CA chat and SMS'}]}>
  <p class="eyebrow">GetPatients.com · A ChiroCandy company</p>
  <h2>Help prospective patients understand your practice</h2>
  <p>People ask search engines and AI assistants questions about local care, services, and providers. AI visibility concerns whether your practice appears in those answers, which sources are cited, and whether the information accurately represents your office. AEO focuses on making useful answers easier to find and understand.</p>
  <p>For a chiropractic practice, the starting point is specific: the services you actually provide, where you provide them, who delivers care, and what a prospective patient should know before contacting you. Clear answers need accurate supporting information.</p>
  <h2>One coordinated plan for SEO and AI visibility</h2>
  <p>Our <a href="/services/search-engine-optimization/">SEO service</a> addresses unpaid search visibility, website content, and local practice information. Those foundations also matter for AI search. The GetPatients.com AI visibility package is a separate offer; review its proposed scope alongside your current agreement before adding it.</p>
  <p>We should identify the work already covered, any additional priorities, who will make each change, and how progress will be reviewed. That makes it possible to coordinate the two services without paying for the same task twice.</p>
  <h2>Discovery, trust, and a clear booking path</h2>
  <p>The GetPatients approach connects three areas. Your proposal defines the priorities for your practice:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Discovery:</strong> review search foundations, service and location information, and how your practice is represented across AI platforms.</li>
    <li><strong>Trust:</strong> make priority service content and answers to patient questions useful, accurate, and specific to your practice.</li>
    <li><strong>Booking readiness:</strong> review mobile usability, calls to action, and appointment information so people can find a clear next step.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Reporting is a service supported by internal tools; client access to a software platform is not included. Booking readiness does not imply a new integration or automated appointment booking.</p>
  <h2>What to discuss during the rollout</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your priority questions:</strong> the services, locations, and patient questions that matter to your practice.</li>
    <li><strong>Your current presence:</strong> your website, local listings, existing content, and available search reporting.</li>
    <li><strong>The proposed work:</strong> deliverables, responsibilities, access requirements, and overlap with your existing marketing.</li>
    <li><strong>The evidence:</strong> how mentions, citations, factual accuracy, inquiries, and appointments will be evaluated.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These are the topics for the planning conversation. Your written proposal establishes the included deliverables, platform coverage, schedule, and fees.</p>
  <h2>Measure visibility and business results separately</h2>
  <p>A useful review records the question, platform, date, and location context of an AI answer, along with any mention or citation. Compare the same questions over time and check whether the answer is accurate. A screenshot of one favorable answer does not establish consistent visibility.</p>
  <p>Then connect visibility with qualified inquiries, booked appointments, and attended visits where reliable tracking exists. No provider controls an AI platform’s recommendations, and a mention alone is not a new patient.</p>
  <p>Read our <a href="/blog/geo-for-chiropractors/">guide to AI search visibility</a> for background, or explore the <a href="/resources/">resource library</a> before the conversation.</p>
  <h2>Discuss AI visibility for your practice</h2>
  <p>Bring your website, service area, current SEO arrangement, and the questions you want patients to find answers to. We’ll discuss the GetPatients.com package and how it fits your practice. Contact us for current rollout details and a proposal.</p>
  <p><a class="btn btn--primary" href="/schedule/">Discuss AI visibility →</a></p>
</ServiceLayout>
